<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">627 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">627 CE in world history: 4 events and 2 deaths. 251 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/554">554 CE</a><a href="/years/602">602 CE</a><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a><a href="/years/626">626 CE</a><a href="/years/627" aria-current="page">627 CE</a><a href="/years/628">628 CE</a><a href="/years/630">630 CE</a><a href="/years/632">632 CE</a><a href="/years/633">633 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">King Edwin of Northumbria is baptised by Paulinus</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Edwin, king of Deira and Bernicia, was baptised with his chief men by Paulinus, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a>. He was the first ruler of both kingdoms to convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria">Edwin of Northumbria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraclius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-12">12 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius defeats the Persians near Nineveh</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> routed a Sasanian army near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The victory ended a 26-year war, but both exhausted empires soon fell prey to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nineveh-627">Battle of Nineveh (627)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Nineveh was fought in 627 CE near the ruins of ancient Nineveh in northern Mesopotamia, where the Byzantine emperor Heraclius defeated a Sasanian army.</p></div></li></ol></section>
